    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\((1+i)^2=2i,\\) we have \\((1+i)^4=-4.\\) Likewise \\((1-i)^2=-2i\\) and \\((1-i)^4=-4.\\) Hence each twentieth power equals \\((-4)^5=-1024,\\) and their difference is \\(0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Compute the fourth power of each conjugate base",
        "Both \\((1+i)^4\\) and \\((1-i)^4\\) equal \\(-4\\)"
      ],
